WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.125 --> 00:00:02.938
For Margaret, going home today means more than

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:04.012
a medical decision.

3
00:00:04.412 --> 00:00:07.750
Her medicines, family and continuing care all need

4
00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:08.400
to be ready.

5
00:00:08.762 --> 00:00:11.350
This is her fictional journey through HomeFlow.

6
00:00:11.750 --> 00:00:13.625
Her nurse begins on Overview.

7
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:17.625
Eighteen discharges are expected across three demonstration wards,

8
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:19.350
and six patients are ready.

9
00:00:19.750 --> 00:00:22.075
The team can see the day's workload before

10
00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:24.125
turning to the person behind one of those

11
00:00:24.138 --> 00:00:24.700
numbers.

12
00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.688
On Ward board, Margaret is in bed twelve,

13
00:00:27.962 --> 00:00:29.200
hoping to leave at two.

14
00:00:29.588 --> 00:00:32.188
She is amber because her take-home medicines are

15
00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.388
still with pharmacy.

16
00:00:33.788 --> 00:00:37.250
The twelve-thirty target and responsible team sit alongside

17
00:00:37.262 --> 00:00:38.688
her expected discharge.

18
00:00:39.062 --> 00:00:41.575
Opening Journey makes the next step clear.

19
00:00:41.962 --> 00:00:45.300
Pharmacy needs to acknowledge her request, and collection

20
00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:46.787
still needs confirmation.

21
00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:50.425
Completed steps and remaining dependencies give her nurse

22
00:00:50.438 --> 00:00:51.988
a shared plan to work from.

23
00:00:52.362 --> 00:00:55.638
Margaret's unfinished action is visible with its deadline

24
00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:56.312
and owner.

25
00:00:56.712 --> 00:00:59.712
If that deadline passes, HomeFlow flags it as

26
00:00:59.725 --> 00:01:00.325
overdue.

27
00:01:00.725 --> 00:01:03.450
In Escalation, her nurse can ask pharmacy to

28
00:01:03.462 --> 00:01:06.825
act, and see whether responsibility has been acknowledged.

29
00:01:07.225 --> 00:01:10.425
The request reaches the separate pharmacy workspace.

30
00:01:10.812 --> 00:01:14.388
Pharmacy acknowledges the escalation and moves her medicines

31
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.475
through preparation.

32
00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:19.462
HomeFlow follows the work; prescribing and clinical checks

33
00:01:19.475 --> 00:01:21.150
stay in the approved systems.

34
00:01:21.550 --> 00:01:24.613
Once her medicines are ready, the stage changes.

35
00:01:25.012 --> 00:01:27.400
Delivery to the ward is recorded, so her

36
00:01:27.412 --> 00:01:29.863
nurse can see progress without another round of

37
00:01:29.875 --> 00:01:30.938
telephone chasing.

38
00:01:31.325 --> 00:01:35.150
Meanwhile, Family helps Margaret's relative plan the afternoon.

39
00:01:35.550 --> 00:01:37.725
Her nurse sends one early alert with the

40
00:01:37.738 --> 00:01:41.025
likely collection time, explaining that final checks may

41
00:01:41.038 --> 00:01:42.200
cause a short delay.

42
00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:44.812
Her relative confirms collection.

43
00:01:45.212 --> 00:01:47.812
That response becomes part of the same discharge

44
00:01:47.825 --> 00:01:50.738
picture, rather than a separate conversation the next

45
00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:52.125
nurse has to rediscover.

46
00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:55.950
Margaret's diabetes plan has changed during admission.

47
00:01:56.325 --> 00:01:59.612
In Handover, the ward chooses the Community Diabetes

48
00:01:59.625 --> 00:02:02.362
Team and shares the verified change and follow-up

49
00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:03.025
request.

50
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.075
An acknowledgement shows that the receiving team has

51
00:02:06.088 --> 00:02:06.688
seen it.

52
00:02:07.088 --> 00:02:09.462
Her story continues beyond the ward.

53
00:02:09.838 --> 00:02:12.500
Now her medicines have arrived and collection is

54
00:02:12.512 --> 00:02:13.262
confirmed.

55
00:02:13.662 --> 00:02:16.175
Back on Ward board, Margaret is green.

56
00:02:16.575 --> 00:02:19.913
HomeFlow's aim is simple: less uncertainty for staff,

57
00:02:20.112 --> 00:02:22.925
a prepared family, and a better coordinated journey

58
00:02:22.938 --> 00:02:23.362
home.

